## Wednesday, September 15, 2010

### Counting to 100 in C++

I started writing this blog post a few days ago, but never got around to finishing it. I've decided to post it now as I was recently asked by a colleague to explain how to count from 1 to 100 in C++. I didn't want to use a for loop since I wanted to demonstrate the use of a while loop.

Here's the code:

int main()
{
int i = 0;
while (i < 100) {
cout << i << " ";
i++;
}
cout << endl;
return 0;
}

The output is:

