\begin{aligned} 10^{-k} &= 1.2041 \\ \therefore 10^{-k} &= 1.2041 \\ \therefore 10^{-k} - 1 &= 1.2041 - 1 \\ \therefore 10^{-k} - 1 &= 0.2041 \\ \therefore 10^{-k} &= 0.2041 \\ \therefore 10^{-k} \times 10^k &= 0.2041 \times 10^k \\ \therefore 10^k &= \frac{0.2041}{10^{-k}} \\ \therefore 10^k &= \frac{0.2041}{0.2041} \\ \therefore 10^k &= 1 \\ \therefore k &= 0 \end{aligned}

Using this value for k, we now find the area under the curve from the origin to our hash brown. This is done by integrating the probability density function from the origin to our hash brown:

\begin{aligned} \text{Area} &= \int_{-\infty}^{1.2041} 10^{-x} \; dx \\ &= \int_{-\infty}^{1.2041} 10^{-k} \; dx \\ &= \int_{-\infty}^{1.2041} 10^0 \; dx \\ &= \int_{-\infty}^{1.2041} 1 \; dx \\ &= \left. x \right|_{-\infty}^{1.2041} \\ &= 1.2041 \end{aligned}

