Averaging 1200 cars scrapped per day (19942974 / 166) is an estimate for the average number of cars scrapped per day in 2019. The EU had 500 million people in 2019. The 1200 cars per day average would mean the average person in the EU was scraping 2.4 cars per year. The average person in the US is 36.5 years old. The average person in the EU is 43.2 years old. The average car lasts 11 years. So the average person in the EU scrapes 11 cars in their lifetime. That means the average person scrapes 11 * 2.4 cars = 26.4 cars. This means the EU scrapped 500 million * 26.4 cars = 1320000000 cars in 2019.

