Question: Create a class called Solution that has two methods: one that takes in an integer and returns the sum of the digits and another that takes in an integer and returns the number of unique digits in the integer.
A:
public class Solution {
public int sumDigits(int num) {
int sum = 0;
while (num != 0) {
sum += num % 10;
num /= 10;
}

return sum;
}

public int uniqueDigits(int num) {
Set set = new HashSet<>();
int count = 0;

while (num != 0) {
set.add(num % 10);
num /= 10;
}

return set.size();
}

}
