We are given the number of birds, N. We want to find the smallest power of ten that is greater than or equal to N. We know that 10^0 is 1, 10^1 is 10, 10^2 is 100, etc.

We can use a loop to find the smallest power of ten that is greater than or equal to N. We can start at 10^1 and keep incrementing until we find the smallest power of ten that is greater than or equal to N. We can use a conditional statement to check if the current power of ten is greater than or equal to N. If it is, we can break out of the loop and return the current power of ten.

